<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-CBA buys government funds manager.</title>
<headline>RTRS-CBA buys government funds manager.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-12-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Commonwealth Bank of Australia CBA) said it had signed contracts for its financial arm, Commonwealth Financial Services (CFM), to purchase Commonwealth Funds Managment Ltd (CFM) from the Federal government.</p>
<p>CFM acts as the wholesale fund manager for a number of public sector retirement income funds.</p>
<p>The bank said CFS was already Australia's second largest retail funds manager and the CFM acquisition enhanced its position in the wholesale market.</p>
<p>Price was unstated.</p>
<p>-- Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
